<title>UK: LPC-Poland's BPH seeks $75 million credit.</title>
<headline>LPC-Poland's BPH seeks $75 million credit.</headline>
<text>
<p>LONDON, January 30 (LPC) - Poland's Bank Przemyslowo-Handlowy (BPH) has mandated Sumitomo Bank to arrange a new $75 million syndicated loan, according to a banker close to the deal.</p>
<p>The five-year credit for this first time borrower is expected to be priced tightly, a banker said.</p>
<p>A recently launched credit for Poland's Amerbank is priced at 85 bps over LIBOR with a three-year maturity.</p>
<p>BPH also has a $100 million convertible bond issue planned for April.</p>
<p>Sophy Tonder 44-0171-542-4048</p>
